      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_46",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Content note: this campaign has minor depictions of blood and gore."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_47",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("It was the thirteenth year of Konrad II’s reign when the strange occurrences in the Estmark Hills on the eastern border of Wesnoth began."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_48",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Cattle and beasts of burden were found dead in the fields and villagers vanished from their houses with nary a clue nor sign of struggle. At first, the settlers suspected raiders from the great desert, but when they sent scouts east they found nothing but a small mountain range and miles of swamp."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_49",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The disappearances did not stop and every day the terror grew greater. Eventually, the people living in the eastern villages sent a messenger to the king, asking for help. The messenger rode hard for many days and nights, and finally reached the city of Weldyn."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_50",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("When the king received news of the problem, his advisor Dacyn had much to say. Apparently, these attacks bore much similarity to ones that had previously occurred on the far southern border where undead had been the eventual culprit. Dacyn outlined a plan to combat these intrusions."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_51",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("In the days of King Garard I, two strong points had been built along the far bank of the River Weldyn, east of Soradoc, to stop bandits and orcish raiders out of the Estmarks from entering Wesnoth. In later years, the river guard posts had been abandoned as colonists spread into the Estmarks and the orcs were driven in retreat north of the Great River."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_52",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("With unknown enemies pressing Wesnoth from the East, Dacyn pressed Konrad II to re-man the outposts, and use them to keep the Crown’s eye and hand firmly on the lower River Weldyn. He sent two of the most promising young officers to them. To the northern outpost he sent Owaec, a Clan noble. To the southern outpost, he sent Sergeant Gweddry, who would be accompanied by Dacyn the mage."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_53",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("All went well once the king’s forces arrived. There were no attacks for several weeks, and Gweddry’s men started to grow incautious. Then, one evening, Gweddry and his men were roused by the startled cries of the night watchmen..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_54",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            units: "Gweddry,Dacyn,Nakeg-alvan,Mal-Talar,u_9,Mel_Guthrak,Gaennell",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
